   'In 1986, Prince Edward, the youngest son of Queen Elizabeth II, commissioned a short musical from Lloyd Webber and Rice for his mother''s 60th birthday celebration.[51] Cricket (1986), also called Cric', 'In 1986, Prince Edward, the youngest son of Queen Elizabeth II, commissioned a short musical from Lloyd Webber and Rice for his mother''s 60th birthday celebration.[51] Cricket (1986), also called Cricket (Hearts and Wickets), reunited Lloyd Webber with Rice to create this short musical for the Queen''s birthday, first performed at Windsor Castle.[52][53] Several of the tunes were later used for Aspects of Love and Sunset Boulevard.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
