   'In 1969, he went 20–13 with a 2.18 ERA, 4 shutouts, and 28 complete games.[21] On May 12, 1969, Gibson struck out three batters on nine pitches in the seventh inning of a 6–2 win over the Los Angeles ', 'In 1969, he went 20–13 with a 2.18 ERA, 4 shutouts, and 28 complete games.[21] On May 12, 1969, Gibson struck out three batters on nine pitches in the seventh inning of a 6–2 win over the Los Angeles Dodgers.[64] Gibson became the ninth National League pitcher and the 15th pitcher in Major League history to throw an immaculate inning.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
