   'He won nine Gold Glove Awards, the National League Cy Young Award in 1968 and 1970, and the National League MVP Award in 1968.[51][74] His 1.12 earned run average and 13 shutouts in 1968 are both reco', 'He won nine Gold Glove Awards, the National League Cy Young Award in 1968 and 1970, and the National League MVP Award in 1968.[51][74] His 1.12 earned run average and 13 shutouts in 1968 are both records in the live-ball era.[75][76]  In his career, Gibson had a win-loss record of 251–174 with an ERA of 2.91.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
