   'And Britney had that."[12] Spears sang Houston''s "I Have Nothing" (1992) for the executives and was subsequently signed to the label.[21] They assigned her to work with producer Eric Foster White for ', 'And Britney had that."[12] Spears sang Houston''s "I Have Nothing" (1992) for the executives and was subsequently signed to the label.[21] They assigned her to work with producer Eric Foster White for a month; he reportedly shaped her voice from a "lower and less poppy" delivery to "distinctively, unmistakably Britney".[22] After hearing the recorded material, president Clive Calder ordered a full album.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
