   'This was not to answer critics from the 1984 long jump controversy; this was because history''s second 29 ft long-jumper was in the field: Robert Emmiyan leapt 8.86 m (29 ft 3⁄4 in) at altitude in May,', 'This was not to answer critics from the 1984 long jump controversy; this was because history''s second 29 ft long-jumper was in the field: Robert Emmiyan leapt 8.86 m (29 ft 3⁄4 in) at altitude in May, just 4 cm short of Bob Beamon''s record.[47] But Emmiyan''s best that day was a leap of 8.53 m (27 ft 11+3⁄4 in), second to Lewis'' 8.67 m (28 ft 5+1⁄4 in).[48] Lewis cleared 8.60 m (28 ft 2+1⁄2 in) four times.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
