  ('ev_wiki_caroline-harrison_1876_7', 'ent_caroline-harrison', NULL, 1876, 'award', 'narrative',
   'He ran an unsuccessful campaign to be the Governor of Indiana in 1876, and he was elected to the United States Senate in 1880.[18] After his election, Caroline oversaw the family''s move to a rented su', 'He ran an unsuccessful campaign to be the Governor of Indiana in 1876, and he was elected to the United States Senate in 1880.[18] After his election, Caroline oversaw the family''s move to a rented suite in Washington, D.C.[29] She served as an advisor in his political career and assisted him in his political campaigns.[30] Her work as a family hostess grew significantly when her husband was chosen as the Republican candidate for the 1888 presidential election.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
