  ('ev_wiki_chief-joseph_1880_18', 'ent_chief-joseph', NULL, 1880, 'personal_life', 'narrative',
   'Wells supports his argument: "The use of military concepts and terms is appropriate when explaining what the whites were doing, but these same military terms should be avoided when referring to Indian', 'Wells supports his argument: "The use of military concepts and terms is appropriate when explaining what the whites were doing, but these same military terms should be avoided when referring to Indian actions; the United States use of military terms such as ''retreat'' and ''surrender'' has created a distorted perception of the Nez Perce War, to understand this may lend clarity to the political and military victories of the Nez Perce."[23]  Aftermath  Chief Joseph and family, c. ', 'src_en_wikipedia',
