  ('ev_wiki_count-basie_1936_9', 'ent_count-basie', '1936-10', 1936, 'personal_life', 'narrative',
   'Many other bands later adapted the split tenor arrangement.[30]  In that city in October 1936, the band had a recording session which the producer John Hammond later described as "the only perfect, co', 'Many other bands later adapted the split tenor arrangement.[30]  In that city in October 1936, the band had a recording session which the producer John Hammond later described as "the only perfect, completely perfect recording session I''ve ever had anything to do with".[31] Hammond first heard Basie''s band on the radio and went to Kansas City to check them out.[32] He invited them to record, in performances which were Lester Young''s earliest recordings.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
