  ('ev_wiki_dalai-lama_1717_24', 'ent_dalai-lama', NULL, 1717, 'death', 'narrative',
   'This plot suited the devious Dzungar leaders'' ambitions and they were only too happy to oblige.[170][171] Early in 1717, after conspiring to undermine Lhazang Khan through treachery they entered Tibet', 'This plot suited the devious Dzungar leaders'' ambitions and they were only too happy to oblige.[170][171] Early in 1717, after conspiring to undermine Lhazang Khan through treachery they entered Tibet from the northwest with a large army, sending a smaller force to Kumbum to collect Kelzang Gyatso and escort him to Lhasa.[172][173]  By the end of the year, with Tibetan connivance they had captured Lhasa, killed Lhazang and all his family and deposed Yeshe Gyatso.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
