  ('ev_wiki_daniel-boone_1771_17', 'ent_daniel-boone', NULL, 1771, 'personal_life', 'narrative',
   'On one occasion, he shot a man to avoid capture, which historian John Mack Faragher says "was one of the few Indians that Boone acknowledged killing."[43] Boone returned to North Carolina in 1771, but', 'On one occasion, he shot a man to avoid capture, which historian John Mack Faragher says "was one of the few Indians that Boone acknowledged killing."[43] Boone returned to North Carolina in 1771, but came back to hunt in Kentucky in the autumn 1772.[44]  In 1773, Boone packed up his family and, with his brother Squire and a group of about 50 others, began the first attempt by British colonists to establish a settlement.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
