   'Some of the settlers forgave Boone the loss; others insisted he repay the stolen money, which took him several years to do.[79]  In contrast to the later folk image of Boone as a backwoodsman who had ', 'Some of the settlers forgave Boone the loss; others insisted he repay the stolen money, which took him several years to do.[79]  In contrast to the later folk image of Boone as a backwoodsman who had little affinity for "civilized" society, Boone was a leading citizen of Kentucky at this time.[80] When Kentucky was divided into three Virginia counties in November 1780, Boone was promoted to lieutenant colonel in the Fayette County militia.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
