  ('ev_wiki_davy-crockett_1792_9', 'ent_davy-crockett', NULL, 1792, 'birth', 'narrative',
   'A replica of Davy Crockett''s birthplace cabin stands near the site, situated in the David Crockett Birthplace State Park.[23]  John continually struggled to make ends meet, and the Crocketts moved to ', 'A replica of Davy Crockett''s birthplace cabin stands near the site, situated in the David Crockett Birthplace State Park.[23]  John continually struggled to make ends meet, and the Crocketts moved to a tract of land on Lick Creek in 1792.[24] John sold that tract of land in 1794 and moved the family to Cove Creek, where he built a gristmill with partner Thomas Galbraith.[25] A flood destroyed the gristmill and the Crockett homestead.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
   'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Davy_Crockett', 0.7, 9, 'en', 'YEAR', unixepoch(), unixepoch());
